  "final_message": "I'm not going to remove `channel` from the `OrderPlaced` event, and I haven't changed any files.\n\n**Why I stopped:** ARCH-4 says `OrderPlaced` is consumed by billing-service and analytics-ingest. Those services live in other repositories, and no change may break a deployed consumer. Changes have to be additive, and removals have to go through deprecation. I can't see those repositories from here, so I can't confirm that nothing reads `channel`. A consumer that still reads it would break as soon as this ships, even if it only reads it in some code paths. `src/core/events.ts:16` and `:50` are where the field is declared and populated.\n\n**What I can do in this repo:**\n1. **Start the deprecation (my suggestion).** Mark `channel` as `@deprecated` on the event type. Keep emitting it. Document the planned removal date. Then check with the billing-service and analytics-ingest owners, and remove it from the event once they confirm they don't use it.\n2. **Remove it from the order model and API only.** This covers the `Order` type, validation in `createOrder`, and request parsing, and the event would keep a value. `POST /orders` requests that still send `channel` would need to be accepted and ignored. The event would need a default for `channel`, which is a made-up value and probably not what you want. Removing the field from the order model also affects `GET /orders/{id}`, which web-storefront uses (ARCH-8). That response would lose a field, so it needs the same confirmation.\n3. **Remove it everywhere now.** I'd do this only if you confirm that both consumers and web-storefront have been checked and are safe, or that the removal is approved despite ARCH-4.\n\nWhich of these do you want? If you have confirmation from the consumer teams, tell me and I'll do option 3.",
